# CLAUDE.md: <FACTORY> ops repo

This repository is the factory as a repo: the specs it builds from, the status it runs on,
the cost it has spent, the ideas it has not yet triaged, and the agents that plan and
judge. Nothing here is a service, and no service code is written here.

## Before anything else

Read `status/current.md`. It is the one record of where the factory is: the active build
track, the next action, the research lane, and what waits on the owner. Every session, in
any repo, reads it first and updates it last.

## Session types

Every session names its type in its first line. The contracts are in the process spec
(`spec/session-types.md` in the factory, vendored into every service as
`docs/process/session-types.md`). The two that start here:

| Task | Type | How it starts |
|---|---|---|
| Improving how the factory works | **system** | `claude --agent system` |
| A problem to research, a spec to write, a stack to choose | **research** | `claude --agent research` |

A planning session runs `planner`, then `scripts/plan-critic-check.sh`, then `plan-critic`,
against an admitted spec and a seeded service repo. An implementation session is never typed
by hand: it is `/run-session <SID>` from the service repo.

## What lives here

| Path | What it is | Its gate |
|---|---|---|
| `specs/` | admitted specs, verbatim, and the ledger of their digests | `scripts/spec-intake-check.sh` (ten rules) |
| `scripts/plan-critic-check.sh` | the plan critic's mechanical half | its fixtures, `gates/plan-critic.test.sh` |
| `status/current.md` | the operating status; its frontmatter feeds the weekday nudge | `scripts/status-render.sh` |
| `status/costs.jsonl` | the spend ledger every driver and reader run appends to | the ceilings in each plan |
| `.claude/agents/` | planner, plan-critic, adr-critic, idea-triage, research, system | |
| `docs/research/`, `docs/adr/` | research briefs and the factory's own decisions | |
| the issue labelled `ideas` | the idea inbox (`/idea <text>` from any repo) | every line accounted for at the weekly review |

`scripts/check.sh` is the gate; CI runs it verbatim, and `gates/check.test.sh` proves it can
fail.

## Rules that hold here

- **One active build track, at most one research lane.**
- **Park at gates, never bypass them.** A decision that is the owner's goes in the decision
  queue in `status/current.md`. A wait on the world is recorded as blocked.
- **Verify artifacts, never self-reports.** A session that cannot show a path, a PR or a URL
  has not done the thing.
- **Specs are admitted verbatim.** A source that does not fit the format is flagged in the
  admission PR, never quietly reshaped.
- **Every flag ships with a default.** Only a flag that cannot be defaulted is `required`,
  with its reason.
- **Telemetry appends to main; code never does.** The spend ledger is the one file machines
  write here without review.
